Subject: [flux] Add the Flux side panel entry

The console had nowhere to live: chrome://flux was reachable by URL and
nothing else. This registers it as a first-class side panel entry, which is
what puts it in the browser shell rather than in a tab.

Four pieces are all mandatory, and each fails differently if left out:

  - SIDE_PANEL_ENTRY_IDS gains kFlux. SidePanelHelper::GetActionItem CHECKs
    that an entry's id maps to an action, so kFlux gets a real ActionId
    rather than the std::nullopt that kWebView and kSidePanelDev use.
  - chrome_action_id.h gains kActionSidePanelShowFlux, with no IDC, the same
    shape as kActionSidePanelShowAssistant.
  - browser_actions.cc builds the ActionItem. Its text is what the side panel
    header and the toolbar button show. IDS_PRODUCT_NAME is the browser's own
    name, which is also the console's - a brand, so nothing to translate.
  - histograms.xml gains a .Flux WebUIName variant. WebUIContentsWrapperT
    static_asserts the name against the allowlist generated from that file,
    so without it this is a compile error, not a missing metric.

The entry itself needs no coordinator: Flux has no per-window state for one
to own, so a free function in side_panel_helper.cc builds the view directly.

